/-!
# The `(5,5)` diagonal graded step in a clash-free import cone

This module proves `Work.SSGRoute.gradedStep_five_five_reduced`, the `(5,5)` diagonal instance of
Schmidt–Wingberg's graded step at `p = 2` for an arbitrary finite group `G` and an involution
`δ ∈ G`, `δ ≠ 1`.

## Route

`tauSucc 5 5 = (6,1)`, so the graded piece is `E(5,5) = ker(Q_{(6,1)} → Q_{(5,5)})`.  Since `5` is
odd, the anti-fixed part of `E(5,5)` agrees with the image of `1 + δ`, and the orbit sums of the
weight-`5` commutator words generate that image:

* `Work.SSGRoute.diagonalCore_odd` (located, for `j = 5`, in the clash-free copy
  `Submission/Work/SSGRoute/FF5/DiagonalPort.lean`): every anti-fixed `c ∈ E(5,5)` lies in the
  subgroup generated by `orbitSumFamily G n 5 δ`.  Its mathematical content is the identification
  `E(j,j) ≅ barLie (Fin n × G) j` (`FF5/EIso.lean`) together with `freeLie_regular_odd`: for odd
  `j` the degree-`j` part of the free `𝔽₂`-Lie algebra on the fixed-point-free involution
  `(a,g) ↦ (a,δg)` has `ker (1+σ) = im (1+σ)`.
* `Work.SSGRoute.orbitSum_is_delta_difference` (`gradedStep_diagonal.lean`): every element of that
  subgroup *is* a `δ`-difference in the ambient group `Q_{(6,1)}` — the graded piece is central of
  exponent `2`, so the defect of the norm map vanishes there.

## The cone

The modules of the original odd-`j` development (`diagonalCore_odd`, `E_iso_barLie`, `EBLPort`,
`diagOdd/theta`) reach `prop5.magnus_leadingTerm`, whose declaration `prop5.magLT` collides with the
`prop5.magLT` of `prop5.adjacent_pSeries_inter_lcs_le` — the latter being unavoidable here (it
enters through `gradedStep_three_three`, which the caller's cone contains).  The `FF5/` directory
therefore holds verbatim copies of exactly that chain with the two import lines redirected
(`prop5.magnus_leadingTerm → prop5.adjacent_pSeries_inter_lcs_le`, the corresponding `magLT_*`
lemmas renamed to their `adj_magLT_*` twins), so the whole argument lives in the clash-free cone.
-/

namespace Work.SSGRoute

open Work.CohomologicalShrinking

theorem gradedStep_five_five_reduced (G : Type*) [Group G] [Fintype G] (n : ℕ) (δ : G)
    (hδ : δ * δ = 1) (hδ1 : δ ≠ 1) :
    ∀ c : Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowQuotient 2 G n
        (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).1
        (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).2,
      Work.SSGRoute.flowQuotSucc 2 G n 5 5 c = 1 →
      Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowAction 2 G n
          (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).1
          (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).2 δ c = c⁻¹ →
      ∃ e : Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowQuotient 2 G n
            (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).1
            (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).2,
        c = (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.flowAction 2 G n
              (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).1
              (Work.CohomologicalShrinking.tauSucc 5 5).2 δ e)⁻¹ * e := by
  intro c hc hanti
  exact orbitSum_is_delta_difference G n 5 δ hδ (by norm_num) c
    (diagonalCore_odd G n δ hδ hδ1 5 (by decide) c hc hanti)

end Work.SSGRoute
